# A declared kind built inside an undeclared one is still built: only the
# undeclared kind is reported, and the paste block lists both.
# error: schema_undeclared_kind_nested.grammar:28:8:
# error: undeclared kind 'foo'
# error:     inner v:leaf
# absent: is declared but no rule builds it
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    integer
    plus
    colon
    comma
    eq
    eof
    err
'+'                                         → plus
':'                                         → colon
','                                         → comma
'='                                         → eq
[0-9]+                                      → integer
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@schema
    inner v:leaf
top! = IDENT                                → (foo (inner 1))
